35
00:02:28.963 --> 00:02:29.859
Part 3.

36
00:02:30.139 --> 00:02:32.123
The Customer Journey, Step by Step.

37
00:02:33.373 --> 00:02:34.375
Opening the app.

38
00:02:34.655 --> 00:02:39.669
App launch: a single home page API call returns a personalised layout.

39
00:02:39.949 --> 00:02:49.826
Widgets such as banners, deals and recently viewed are chosen by a content or widget platform that marketing configures for sales without code deployments.

40
00:02:50.106 --> 00:02:52.197
Personalisation ranks the widgets.

41
00:02:52.477 --> 00:02:53.309
Caching:

42
00:02:53.589 --> 00:02:58.879
Static assets and images come from the CDN in sizes appropriate to the device.

43
00:03:00.229 --> 00:03:05.904
Personalised parts are fetched separately from cacheable parts, so most bytes are cacheable at the edge.

44
00:03:06.184 --> 00:03:15.272
Device constraints: for low-end devices and slow networks, the app or PWA downloads less (fewer widgets, lower-resolution images).

45
00:03:15.552 --> 00:03:21.397
Flipkart publicly launched a PWA, Flipkart Lite, in 2015 (VERIFY).

46
00:03:22.747 --> 00:03:25.222
Searching in Hindi, Hinglish or by voice.

47
00:03:25.502 --> 00:03:31.347
The query can be typed in English, Hindi script, Latin-script Hindi (mobail cover) or spoken.

48
00:03:31.627 --> 00:03:35.105
Speech: voice input goes through speech recognition to text.

49
00:03:35.385 --> 00:03:39.907
Flipkart has publicly discussed vernacular voice search (VERIFY details).

50
00:03:40.187 --> 00:03:52.326
Query understanding: transliteration and normalisation to a common representation;. spell correction trained on Indian spelling patterns;. vernacular-to-English mapping for catalog terms;.

51
00:03:53.676 --> 00:03:59.372
category and attribute prediction (for example, under 15000 becomes a price filter).

52
00:03:59.652 --> 00:04:09.465
Retrieval: lexical matches from an inverted index;. semantic retrieval with multilingual embeddings;. filtered by serviceability to the user's pincode.

53
00:04:10.815 --> 00:04:18.474
Ranking: learning-to-rank on relevance, conversion history, price competitiveness, delivery speed, ratings and seller quality.

54
00:04:18.754 --> 00:04:21.698
Sponsored listings are blended through the ads auction.

55
00:04:23.048 --> 00:04:24.179
The product page.

56
00:04:24.459 --> 00:04:42.912
Components: catalog content (possibly translated);. the chosen seller's offer (a buy-box-like selection among sellers, similar to I01);. price with sale discount;. bank offers and EMI options (estimated);. exchange offers;. delivery date for the user's pincode;.

57
00:04:44.262 --> 00:04:50.193
COD availability;. ratings and reviews;. questions and answers;. recommendations.

58
00:04:50.473 --> 00:05:01.097
Pincode check: the serviceability service answers from precomputed tables: pincode times seller or warehouse times product size or weight class times payment type;.

59
00:05:02.447 --> 00:05:05.647
result: can we deliver, by when, and is COD allowed.

60
00:05:06.997 --> 00:05:08.149
Cart and checkout.

61
00:05:08.429 --> 00:05:10.967
Cart: the cart stores items and quantities.

62
00:05:11.247 --> 00:05:13.701
It can be merged across devices at login.

63
00:05:13.981 --> 00:05:23.047
Checkout: address selection, with address quality checks: pincode validation, geocoding, and prompts for missing landmarks;. serviceability re-check.

64
00:05:23.327 --> 00:05:25.567
Price computation: sale price;.

65
00:05:26.917 --> 00:05:36.667
coupon;. bank offer once the payment instrument is known;. coins or loyalty redemption;. delivery fee rules;. taxes (GST per item and seller).

66
00:05:36.947 --> 00:05:38.077
Payment options:

67
00:05:38.357 --> 00:05:51.605
UPI (intent or collect), cards (tokenised), net banking, EMI (card EMI, cardless EMI or pay later), wallets and gift cards, and COD if the risk score allows (I02 L2).

68
00:05:52.955 --> 00:06:09.510
Order placement: reservation of stock from the chosen warehouse or seller;. payment authorisation (or COD confirmation flow);. order created with the promise, the fulfilment plan and price breakdown lines (who funds each discount: seller, platform or bank).

69
00:06:10.860 --> 00:06:11.713
Payments.

70
00:06:11.993 --> 00:06:22.105
Routing: a payments orchestrator routes each transaction to a gateway or processor by method, bank and live success rates (Ch 45 L4).

71
00:06:22.385 --> 00:06:32.945
UPI flows: intent (opens a UPI app) or collect (request in the UPI app), with status polling and callbacks; see I03 for the bank side.

72
00:06:33.225 --> 00:06:36.767
EMI and pay later: eligibility checks with lenders.

73
00:06:37.047 --> 00:06:40.780
The platform may partner with lenders for credit products (VERIFY).

74
00:06:41.060 --> 00:06:43.620
Refunds go to the source instrument or wallet.

75
00:06:43.900 --> 00:06:48.913
Reconciliation against gateway and bank settlement files, as in Ch 45.

76
00:06:50.263 --> 00:06:52.525
Order management and fulfilment choice.

77
00:06:52.805 --> 00:06:59.162
The order management system (OMS) splits the order into shipments by seller, warehouse and size class.

78
00:06:59.442 --> 00:07:07.762
Each shipment is a state machine: created, then packed, then dispatched, then in transit, then out for delivery, then delivered or RTO.

79
00:07:08.042 --> 00:07:22.122
Fulfilment models: platform warehouses hold seller inventory (a fulfilment-by-platform model; Flipkart's Flipkart Assured signals quality and fast delivery, VERIFY);. seller-fulfilled items are picked up from the seller.

80
00:07:23.472 --> 00:07:26.053
Cancellation is allowed until dispatch.

81
00:07:26.333 --> 00:07:29.747
Payment is authorised or captured according to the method.

82
00:07:31.097 --> 00:07:33.315
Warehouses and the logistics network.

83
00:07:33.595 --> 00:07:38.331
Warehouses (fulfilment centres): inbound from sellers, stow, pick, pack.

84
00:07:38.611 --> 00:07:42.302
Large-appliance warehouses are separate from small-item ones.

85
00:07:42.582 --> 00:07:46.977
Sortation is automated at big sites (VERIFY specific automation).

86
00:07:47.257 --> 00:07:55.385
Network: fulfilment centre, then mother hubs (large sortation), then delivery hubs near pincode clusters, then delivery agents.

87
00:07:55.665 --> 00:08:03.601
This is a hub-and-spoke network run by the in-house logistics arm (Ekart; VERIFY current structure) plus third-party couriers.

88
00:08:03.881 --> 00:08:08.211
Line-haul: truck schedules between hubs, planned from volume forecasts.

89
00:08:08.491 --> 00:08:11.158
Sale periods add temporary hubs and vehicles.

90
00:08:12.508 --> 00:08:25.415
Last mile: shipments assigned to delivery agents by area;. route optimisation (VRP with time windows and capacity);. agent app with navigation, proof of delivery (OTP, photo);.

91
00:08:25.695 --> 00:08:28.447
COD cash collection and UPI-at-door.

92
00:08:28.727 --> 00:08:31.671
COD cash: agents deposit cash at hubs.

93
00:08:31.951 --> 00:08:34.639
Cash is reconciled per shipment and remitted.

94
00:08:34.919 --> 00:08:39.463
Mismatches are investigated (Ch 45 §2.7).

95
00:08:40.813 --> 00:08:44.269
Failed deliveries: re-attempt scheduling, customer calls.

96
00:08:44.549 --> 00:08:47.855
If it still fails, RTO back to the warehouse or seller.

97
00:08:49.205 --> 00:08:50.080
Returns.

98
00:08:50.360 --> 00:08:56.291
Return request: reason captured; policy checked (return, replacement, or not returnable).

99
00:08:56.571 --> 00:09:03.589
Reverse pickup: scheduled, with doorstep quality checks for some categories (for example, matching IMEI for phones).

100
00:09:03.869 --> 00:09:08.669
Refund: issued on pickup or on receipt, depending on the customer's trust tier.

101
00:09:08.949 --> 00:09:14.432
Returned item: graded at the warehouse, then restocked, returned to the seller, or refurbished.

102
00:09:15.782 --> 00:09:17.019
Customer support.

103
00:09:17.299 --> 00:09:22.249
Self-service first: order tracking, cancellation, returns and refund status.

104
00:09:22.529 --> 00:09:28.246
Chat: a chatbot with intent classification, handing off to agents with full order context.

105
00:09:28.526 --> 00:09:30.787
Voice support in multiple languages.

106
00:09:31.067 --> 00:09:34.481
Operations: support tickets link to orders and shipments.

107
00:09:34.761 --> 00:09:41.758
Common issues are auto-resolved by rules, for example, refunding automatically when a shipment is marked lost.

108
