211
00:14:03.583 --> 00:14:04.607
Deep Dives.

212
00:14:05.857 --> 00:14:09.355
5A.1 How the search index is built and kept fresh.

213
00:14:09.635 --> 00:14:19.577
Source events: catalog changes (new listing, attribute edit), offer changes (price, stock, seller) and serviceability changes all emit events.

214
00:14:19.857 --> 00:14:25.595
Document assembly: an indexing pipeline joins these into a search document per product.

215
00:14:25.875 --> 00:14:33.363
It holds: title and attributes;. vernacular and transliterated variants;. category path;. best price and discount;.

216
00:14:34.713 --> 00:14:41.433
rating;. seller-quality score;. availability by region (bitmaps or lists of serviceable warehouse clusters).

217
00:14:41.713 --> 00:14:54.705
Two update paths: real-time partial updates for price and stock, within seconds, so sold-out items don't rank;. periodic full rebuilds (for example, nightly) for text and embedding changes.

218
00:14:56.055 --> 00:15:01.815
Blue-green index aliases switch rebuilt indexes in without downtime (Ch 22).

219
00:15:02.095 --> 00:15:08.709
Embeddings: product embeddings are recomputed in batch by the ML platform and pushed to the vector index.

220
00:15:08.989 --> 00:15:11.314
Query embeddings are computed online.

221
00:15:11.594 --> 00:15:15.989
Serving: search nodes shard the index by product and replicate each shard.

222
00:15:16.269 --> 00:15:25.165
A query fans out to shards, merges top-K, then re-ranks with the heavier model on the top few hundred (Ch 42 for autocomplete).

223
00:15:26.515 --> 00:15:29.203
5A.2 How recommendations are produced.

224
00:15:29.483 --> 00:15:30.976
Candidate generation.

225
00:15:31.256 --> 00:15:47.427
Several cheap sources each propose hundreds of items: co-view and co-buy item-to-item tables (precomputed daily);. embedding nearest neighbours of recently viewed items;. trending in the user's city;. category affinity;. continue where you left off.

226
00:15:48.777 --> 00:16:00.105
Ranking: one model scores all candidates with user features, item features, context (time, device, language, sale day) and cross features, trained on clicks and purchases.

227
00:16:00.385 --> 00:16:16.278
Re-ranking: business rules and diversity, such as: not five similar phones in a row;. boosting in-stock items that are fast to deliver to this pincode;. removing out-of-stock or non-serviceable items;. frequency caps for sponsored items.

228
00:16:17.628 --> 00:16:35.719
Serving: precomputed recommendations for the home page are stored per user in a key-value store, so reading them is a single lookup;. real-time signals (the last few views in this session) re-rank at request time;. everything degrades to popular-in-category if the model service is slow.

229
00:16:35.999 --> 00:16:36.873
Measurement:

230
00:16:37.153 --> 00:16:42.444
A or B tests on conversion and revenue per session, and guardrails on page latency.

231
00:16:43.794 --> 00:16:47.485
5A.3 How serviceability and the promise are computed.

232
00:16:47.765 --> 00:17:04.703
Inputs: courier and own-logistics coverage per pincode;. hub mappings;. transit time matrices (origin hub, then destination hub, hub, then pincode);. cut-off times;. capacity per hub per day;. product constraints (weight, size, hazardous items, high value);.

233
00:17:06.053 --> 00:17:08.848
payment constraints (COD limits per pincode).

234
00:17:09.128 --> 00:17:21.395
Precompute: a batch job builds a table: origin warehouse cluster times destination pincode times product class, then serviceable, promise days, COD allowed, courier options.

235
00:17:21.675 --> 00:17:30.421
It is loaded into a low-latency key-value store and refreshed several times a day, plus immediately on disruptions (hub closure, floods).

236
00:17:30.701 --> 00:17:40.941
At request time: find warehouses holding stock for the product, look up each (warehouse, pincode, class), and choose the fastest serviceable option with capacity.

237
00:17:41.221 --> 00:17:44.656
The result is the Delivery by Tuesday and COD flag.

238
00:17:46.006 --> 00:17:52.427
Feedback: actual delivery times feed back into transit-time estimates, so promises reflect reality.

239
00:17:52.707 --> 00:17:55.523
Promise accuracy is tracked per pincode and hub.

240
00:17:56.873 --> 00:17:59.881
5A.4 Inside a warehouse (WMS).

241
00:18:00.161 --> 00:18:05.495
Inbound: receive against the seller's advance shipping notice, with quality checks per category.

242
00:18:05.775 --> 00:18:10.489
Put-away and slotting: fast-moving items go to locations close to packing.

243
00:18:10.769 --> 00:18:14.268
Slotting is recomputed by sales velocity before sales.

244
00:18:14.548 --> 00:18:19.775
Order release in waves: orders are grouped by dispatch cut-off and destination hub.

245
00:18:20.055 --> 00:18:26.241
Picking: batch picking: one picker collects items for many orders, then they are sorted to orders (put-wall);.

246
00:18:27.591 --> 00:18:29.554
pick paths are optimised per zone.

247
00:18:29.834 --> 00:18:34.890
Packing: box recommendation by item dimensions; invoice and label printing.

248
00:18:35.170 --> 00:18:41.207
Sortation: sorted by destination hub into bags or cages, then manifested per truck.

249
00:18:41.487 --> 00:18:49.594
Sale preparation: pre-packing of hot deal items before the sale (packed and labelled once the order arrives), and extra shifts.

250
00:18:50.944 --> 00:18:53.760
5A.5 A sale-day request, end to end.

251
00:18:54.040 --> 00:19:01.592
Before the unlock: the user opens the deal page from the CDN, and the app syncs to server time (I02 L1).

252
00:19:01.872 --> 00:19:11.365
Buy: the tap goes through the gateway (bot checks, rate limits) into the waiting room, which admits the user at checkout's sustainable rate (Ch 46).

253
00:19:11.645 --> 00:19:18.493
Checkout: the deal quantity is reserved from bucketed stock;. the household limit is checked (I02 L4);.

254
00:19:19.843 --> 00:19:26.478
the price is computed with bank offers, the offer budget reserved, the payment authorised, and the order created.

255
00:19:26.758 --> 00:19:35.590
Events: order events flow to OMS, the warehouse release queue, notifications, and the real-time sale dashboard via stream processing.

256
00:19:35.870 --> 00:19:38.686
Fulfilment: pre-packed items ship within hours.

257
00:19:38.966 --> 00:19:44.107
Logistics hubs run extended shifts, and customers see live tracking from scan events.

258
00:19:45.457 --> 00:19:48.145
5A.6 Loyalty coins and membership.

259
00:19:48.425 --> 00:19:51.945
Coins are earned on orders and credited after the return window.

260
00:19:52.225 --> 00:19:56.236
They are redeemable on later orders and partner offers, and expire.

261
00:19:56.516 --> 00:20:05.689
Accounting: a ledger per customer, where earning, redemption, expiry and reversal on return are all entries (Ch 45 patterns).

262
00:20:05.969 --> 00:20:08.380
Coin liability is tracked by finance.

263
00:20:08.660 --> 00:20:12.905
Membership tiers unlock benefits (early sale access, free delivery).

264
00:20:13.185 --> 00:20:17.367
Tier eligibility is computed from spend or coins over a window.

